            "analysis": "The only measurement is a valid 4-case ARM64 baseline at 0.133006465 s; there is no profile or prior optimized result. This program emits every distinct permutation, so output work grows factorially. The source performs many stream insertions per line and calls `std::endl` for every permutation, making buffered exact serialization the strongest initial hypothesis. Parallel generation is uncertain because lexicographic output must remain globally ordered and stdout is serial. All candidates must remain correct for every valid input and preserve the source’s observable behavior exactly."
